2. C# Guessing Game Program

CODE:

csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Random random = new Random();

        int secretNumber = random.Next(1, 101);
        int guess = 0;
        int attempts = 0;

        Console.WriteLine("Guess the number from 1 to 100");

        while (guess != secretNumber)
        {
            Console.Write("Enter your guess: ");
            guess = Convert.ToInt32(Console.ReadLine());

            attempts++;

            if (guess < secretNumber)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Too low!");
            }
            else if (guess > secretNumber)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Too high!");
            }
            else
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Correct!");
                Console.WriteLine("You got it in " + attempts + " tries.");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

SIMPLE EXPLANATION:

- using System;
  This allows us to use basic C# commands like `Console`.

- class Program
  This is where we put our program.

- static void Main()
  This is where the program starts.

- Random random = new Random();
  This creates a random number generator.

- int secretNumber = random.Next(1, 101);
  This creates a random number from 1 to 100.

- int guess = 0;
  This stores the number that the user will guess.

- int attempts = 0;
  This counts how many times the user guesses.

- while (guess != secretNumber)
  This makes the program continue until the user gets the correct number.

- Console.Write()
  This displays a message and lets the user type their answer.

- Convert.ToInt32(Console.ReadLine())
  This gets the user's input and changes it into a number.

- attempts++;
  This adds 1 to the number of attempts.

-`if (guess < secretNumber)
  Checks if the guess is lower than the secret number.

- else if (guess > secretNumber)
  Checks if the guess is higher than the secret number.

- else 
  This means the guess is correct.
